@@ -188,3 +188,17 @@
 
 In place of queues, AnyIO offers a more powerful construct:
 :ref:`memory object streams <memory object streams>`.
+
+Module-level synchronization objects
+------------------------------------
+
+Events and capacity limiters can be constructed without a running event loop.
+An Event can be set and inspected before use; its flag persists across sequential
+event loop runs. Cancelling a waiter does not set the Event.
+
+A CapacityLimiter constructed outside an event loop keeps one pool across
+sequential runs. Explicit borrowers can reserve and release tokens synchronously
+outside a loop and retain them between runs, including runs on different backends.
+Reducing the limit does not revoke tokens. Queued acquisitions are FIFO; granted
+slots are reserved until resumed or cancelled. Cancellation recovers the slot.
+Concurrent use from multiple event loops or threads is not supported.
